{
  "root_node": "model.fct_orders",
  "cause": "code_change",
  "action": "patch",
  "evidence": "The not_null test on fct_orders.region_name failed with 14,625 nulls (out of 15,000 rows). In fct_orders, region_name is sourced from dim_customers via a left join: `left join {{ ref('dim_customers') }} c on o.order_key = c.customer_key`. This join uses o.order_key instead of o.customer_key, causing only 375 rows to match (verified by `select count(*) from staging.stg_orders o join marts.dim_customers c on o.order_key = c.customer_key` = 375). Consequently, 14,625 rows have null region_name. The upstream tables (raw.orders, staging.stg_orders, dim_customers) have expected row counts and no nulls in region_name. The issue originates from the incorrect join condition in the fct_orders model, a code error. Fix by changing the join to `on o.customer_key = c.customer_key`."
}
